From b6651f86854c0c0f7cb5c7e15672aab47913cc32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:56:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/23] vulkan: batched multi-column mul_mat_vec, strided B,
 AMD large-WG knobs; GLM verify-shape tests

- mul_mat_vec shaders step between B/D columns with stride_b/stride_d instead of the batch strides, so
  2-4 columns work together with ne12*ne13 batches (batched MLA absorb at a 3-token verify ran as a GEMM:
  q8_0 m=256 k=512 batch=64 n=3 87.8 -> 47.1 us, m=512 k=256 81.2 -> 59.2 us cold)
- f32 B with contiguous rows and aligned strides (0213-permuted activations) is read in place
- GGML_VK_DISABLE_BATCHED_MMV, GGML_VK_DMMV_LARGE_MAX_M / _MIN_K experiment knobs (AMD workgroup size)
- test-backend-ops: test_mul_mat_glm with GLM-5.3-Flash decode shapes at n=1..4, plus cold-cache perf
  variants (distinct weights beyond the 32 MiB MALL; time with GGML_VK_PERF_LOGGER)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a8b80faa38bcd73b6f0cc56984defb53d16d30d6)
